### P2  ANKENY-ARTIN-CHOWLA
Statement (Ankeny-Artin-Chowla, Ann. of Math. 56 (1952); CITED): for a prime p = 1 (mod 4) with fundamental
  unit (t + u sqrt p)/2 of Q(sqrt p), p does not divide u.
S7 FINITE-EXACT (PARI quadunit, ring of discriminant p): 211 primes p = 1 mod 4 in [5, 3000).
    norm t^2 - p u^2 in {+4,-4} for all: True (norm -4 count: 211, +4 count: 0)
    AAC violations (u = 0 mod p): none
    largest 3-adic valuations of u:  p=5 v3=0 (u has 1 digits), p=13 v3=0 (u has 1 digits), p=17 v3=0 (u has 1 digits), p=29 v3=0 (u has 1 digits), p=37 v3=0 (u has 1 digits), p=41 v3=0 (u has 2 digits), p=53 v3=0 (u has 1 digits), p=61 v3=0 (u has 1 digits)
    largest 2-adic valuations of u:  p=17 v2=1 (u has 1 digits), p=37 v2=1 (u has 1 digits), p=41 v2=1 (u has 2 digits), p=73 v2=1 (u has 3 digits), p=89 v2=1 (u has 3 digits), p=97 v2=1 (u has 4 digits), p=101 v2=1 (u has 1 digits), p=113 v2=1 (u has 3 digits)
    histogram v3(u): {0: 211}
    histogram v2(u): {0: 79, 1: 132}
    expected for a 'random' integer: P(v3>=k)=3^-k, P(v2>=k)=2^-k; counts >= : v3>=1: 0 (70.3 expected), v3>=2: 0 (23.4), v2>=1: 132 (105.5), v2>=2: 0 (52.8)
    longest u: p=2689 with 38 digits; u mod p = 2646
S7b PROVED (why the histograms are degenerate): the fundamental unit of Q(sqrt p), p = 1 mod 4 prime, has norm -1
    (CITED classical: Legendre/Dirichlet; re-seen: 211 of 211 above), so t^2 - p u^2 = -4.
    mod 3: 3 | u would give t^2 = -4 = 2 mod 3, impossible; hence v3(u) = 0 ALWAYS.
    mod 16: 4 | u would give t^2 = -4 = 12 mod 16, impossible; hence v2(u) <= 1 ALWAYS.
    mod 8: t,u both odd forces 1 - p = -4 mod 8, i.e. p = 5 mod 8; so p = 1 mod 8 forces v2(u) = 1 (unit lies in Z[sqrt p]).
    Census: p = 1 mod 8: 101 primes, all with v2(u)=1: True;  p = 5 mod 8: 110 primes, v2(u)=0 for 79 of them, v2(u)=1 for 31.
    So 'large 2-adic or 3-adic valuation of u' cannot occur for ANY p: the only honest bridge to the session's 2/3-adic
    objects is closed by the norm equation itself.  Nothing Collatz-like appears.
S8 CITED: AAC verified for all p < 2*10^11 (van der Poorten, te Riele, Williams, Math. Comp. 70 (2001) and its 2003 corrigendum).
    UNCITED-RECOLLECTION (not asserted): a 2024 preprint claiming a counterexample; not checked here.
S9 SCOPE / NO MAP: no object of the session is a unit of a real quadratic field of prime discriminant p = 1 mod 4.
    The Pell hypotenuses of THM-3341 are units of Z[sqrt 2] (discriminant 8): p=2 is excluded from AAC.
    'Silver ratio', 'Fermat numbers 2^(2^r)+1', 'repunit prime breaks', 'reversed Hamiltonian edge': no map found.

