S11 PROVED (one line): if alpha has unbounded partial quotients then for every beta,
    liminf n ||n alpha|| ||n beta|| <= liminf q_i ||q_i alpha|| * 1/2 <= liminf 1/(2 a_{i+1}) = 0.
    Whether log_2 3 has unbounded partial quotients is OPEN (as for every non-quadratic algebraic-or-transcendental
    constant not of Euler/e type); the pair (log_2 3, phi) is therefore OPEN, and phi = [1;1,1,...] has BOUNDED quotients,
    so nothing about phi helps.
