### P4  SARNAK
Statement (Sarnak 2009/2010, CITED): for every zero-entropy topological dynamical system (X,T), every f in C(X)
  and every x in X, (1/N) sum_{n<=N} mu(n) f(T^n x) -> 0.
S14 CITED: the map T(x)=x/2 (even), (3x+1)/2 (odd) on Z_2 is topologically conjugate, via the parity-vector map Q,
    to the one-sided full 2-shift (Lagarias 1985, Bernstein-Lagarias 1996); h_top = log 2 = 0.693147.
    The greedy 3-adic map G of this session is conjugate to a 6-state SFT of entropy log 3 = 1.098612
    (three_adic_g_map lane, Theorem 1.3).  Both have positive entropy: Sarnak's hypothesis fails; no statement follows.
S15 PROVED + FINITE-EXACT: Q is a bijection, so there is a 2-adic x with parity(x) = 0 and parity(T^k x) = [mu(k) = 1] for ALL k >= 1.
    Truncation: x = 1781862506 mod 2^32 realises parity(x)=0 and the first 31 values of [mu=1]: 01000010001000110000011000100000
    For that x, f(T^n x) = parity(T^n x) = [mu(n)=1] for n >= 1, so (1/N) sum_{n<=N} mu(n) f(T^n x) = (1/N) #{n<=N : mu(n)=1} -> 3/pi^2 = 0.303964, not 0:
    Mobius disjointness is FALSE for the Collatz system on Z_2 (as for any full shift).  Such x is not in Q: rational 2-adic
    integers have eventually periodic parity vectors (Lagarias 1985, CITED) and [mu=1] is not eventually periodic (every
    class r mod P contains infinitely many n with mu(n)=1 and infinitely many with mu(n)=0).
S16 FINITE-EXACT (N=1000000): c_j = (1/N) sum_{n<=N} mu(n) (-1)^{parity(T^j n)}, and the periodicity check mod 2^(j+1).
    j=0  c_j = -0.000068   parity mean = 0.500000   parity(T^j n) periodic mod 2: True
    j=1  c_j = +0.000344   parity mean = 0.500000   parity(T^j n) periodic mod 4: True
    j=2  c_j = +0.000306   parity mean = 0.500000   parity(T^j n) periodic mod 8: True
    j=3  c_j = +0.000086   parity mean = 0.500000   parity(T^j n) periodic mod 16: True
    j=4  c_j = -0.000054   parity mean = 0.500000   parity(T^j n) periodic mod 32: True
    j=5  c_j = +0.000600   parity mean = 0.500000   parity(T^j n) periodic mod 64: True
    j=6  c_j = -0.000760   parity mean = 0.499992   parity(T^j n) periodic mod 128: True
    PROVED (via CITED PNT in arithmetic progressions, Landau; the periodicity mod 2^(j+1) is Terras 1976 / Everett 1977, CITED,
    and is sharp: not periodic mod 2^j, see the audit): each c_j -> 0 because parity(T^j n) is periodic mod 2^(j+1),
    hence a finite combination of residue-class indicators, each Mobius-orthogonal.  This is the zero-entropy rotation on
    Z/2^(j+1), not the Collatz dynamics, and says nothing about Collatz.
S17 SCOPE / NO MAP: 'F=S+U' is the divisor identity F=S+U iff N in {p,p^3,p^2qr} (divisor_balance lane); the 4-vertex
    tournament matrix is the cell_ordering lane's score-profile object; B^3=-I is THM-4139's lift of the 3-cycle of
    x^2-29/16 (zsigmondy_triad lane).  None is a dynamical system on which mu acts; no 'trapping loop' is defined.

### P5  THE BOX RING AND THE COPRIME FIBRES
S18 PROVED: a boxtimes b := ab+a+b satisfies (a boxtimes b)+1 = (a+1)(b+1) (checked on [-10,10]^2, 0 failures).
    With a boxplus b := a+b+1 the map x -> x+1 is a ring ISOMORPHISM (Z, boxplus, boxtimes) -> (Z, +, *);
    zero is -1, one is 0, the diagonal a boxtimes a = a^2+2a = (a+1)^2-1.  Transport preserves everything and adds nothing.
S19 REFUTED (as a map): R(x)=4x+1 is not c boxtimes x = (c+1)x+c for any c (needs c+1=4 and c=1): solutions c in [-50,50]: []
S20 PROVED (inherited braid): x_j = 4^j x_0 + (4^j-1)/3 = R^j(x_0); gcd(x_j, x_{j+1}) = gcd(x_j, 4x_j+1) = 1 (max over j<30, x_0=7: 1).
S21 PROVED: consecutive odd iterates x, x' = (3x+1)/2^k satisfy gcd(x,x') | gcd(x,3x+1) = 1 (checked on 326623 pairs, max gcd 1).
    Both are odd, so the pair is a point of the odd-coprime chart (s,t)=(m+n,m-n) of the pythagorean_semicircle lane,
    i.e. it determines one PPT ((s^2-t^2)/2, st, (s^2+t^2)/2) after ordering; that is the orbit-PPT lane's input.
    For Giuga it is content-free (S6).

